From 3607dd7f17db72da3fd1194ed62aaf7d73f73f6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:24:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 58/65] nxhost: bsd SendMMsg/RecvMMsg, so Splatoon 3's gRPC can
 talk to NPLN

Splatoon 3's gRPC writes and reads its TCP stream with sendmsg/recvmsg, which
the SDK sends as bsd cmd 30 (SendMMsg) and 29 (RecvMMsg). Both were stubs:
the game re-sent its TLS ClientHello ~850,000 times and never left the
loading screen. They now parse the serialized mmsghdr array in the in/out
buffer, as observed: per message u32 8, u8 0 (no address), u32 iov count,
per iov u64 length + data (the room to fill, for recv), then a 12-byte
trailer whose last u32 receives the message's byte count.

NX_NEXTENDO_SERVER overrides the Nextendo server address for the redirects,
for testing against a local server.

Tested in a sandbox that only reaches localhost, with a local TLS server:
TLS 1.2 with ALPN h2 completes, and the game sends its first gRPC call,
/nn.npln.auth.v1.Auth/IssuePrearrangedUserToken, to the NPLN tenant.
